.TH zmon "" "Command"
.SH NAME
zmon \- GUI system monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBzmon [\fIoptions\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
zmon -- GUI system monitor
Usage:	zmon [ options ]
Keys:	^P/^N scroll process list, ^Z/^V page, Space page down
.HE
.B zmon
is the system monitor of the
.SM COHERENT
GUI.
It must be run under the
.B zview
desktop.
Every 3 seconds it takes a snapshot of the kernel through
.B /dev/kmem
and redraws what changed: a memory total line, a bar of user memory
in use, a breakdown grid (kernel, arena, buffers, segments, stacks,
system, shared, saving, free, holes, largest), and a process list
in
.B ps
style \- PID, user, size, tty, state, time and command.
The display is read-only; there is no way to signal or kill a
process from it.
.B zmon
accepts the standard window
.I options
of GUI applications; see
.BR zview .
.PP
The only keys scroll the process list:
.DS
.ta 6n 22n
	\fB^P, ^N\fR	up / down one line
	\fB^Z, ^B\fR	up one page
	\fB^V, ^F, SPACE\fR	down one page
.DE
The state column shows
.B R
running,
.B S
sleeping,
.B W
waiting,
.B T
stopped and
.B Z
defunct.
Command lines that cannot be read show as
.BR <defunct> ,
.BR <idle> ,
.B <swap>
or
.BR <slib> .
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 8n 30n
	/coherent	kernel image, for the symbol table
	/dev/kmem	kernel memory (required)
	/dev/mem, /dev/swap	command lines (optional)
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR zview ,
.B ps
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
When the kernel cannot be read, the memory pane shows
`Memory: no data' with the reason beneath:
`(bad namelist in /coherent)',
`(cannot open /dev/kmem)',
`(kernel memory read error)',
`(out of memory)'.
.SH NOTES
Reading
.B /dev/kmem
requires the usual permission; without it
.B zmon
runs but shows no data.
Without
.B /dev/mem
only the command column degrades.
At most 96 processes are shown.
The refresh interval is fixed.
